  "issue_comments": [
    {
      "body": "I went to resolve the conflict here and I don't think this change is needed on main anymore.\n\nThe crash in #2129 came from mbridge's `_build_base_config` passing `rotary_percent` straight into `TransformerConfig(**base_config)`. #2251 removed mbridge, including `slime_plugins/mbridge/minimax_m2.py`, and `tools/convert_hf_to_torch_dist.py` no longer goes through `AutoBridge`. The config now comes from `core_transformer_config_from_args` in `model_provider.py`. At the pinned Megatron commit (4b4acac) that helper only copies fields `TransformerConfig` declares, so an unexpected keyword can't reach it. `rotary_percent` goes to `GPTModel` as a constructor argument instead, so the `--rotary-percent 0.5` in `scripts/models/minimax-m2.sh` still takes effect.\n\nThe patches moved on too. `docker/patch/latest` and `v0.5.21` no longer touch `transformer_config.py`, so the hunk has nowhere to land, and the older version directories aren't what the default `PATCH_VERSION` builds.\n\nI checked this by reading main at 540ea91, I didn't run a MiniMax-M2 conversion. Anyone still seeing this error on an older checkout should be fixed by updating slime and the image.\n\n<!-- r:f389ef1b76de.ff43a9a2b777 -->",
      "created_at": "2026-10-31T11:46:44Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/THUDM/slime/pull/2190#issuecomment-6542952800",
      "id": 6542952800,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-31T11:46:44Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "mvanhorn"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "Closing this as superseded, for the reason in my note above. If you'd still like any of it, say so and I'll port it onto current main.",
